radeonsi/ac: sample GFX7-8 stencil through the DB copy when its macro tile mode differs from depth's

On GFX7-8 the DB applies the depth plane's macro tile mode (bank width, bank
height, macro tile aspect, from DB_DEPTH_INFO) to both planes, while the
texture unit derives the stencil plane's macro tile mode from the stencil
tiling index. matchStencilTileCfg keeps the two equal only for mipmapped
Z/S and Stoney. With TC-compatible HTILE on MSAA, depth takes a tile split
that no stencil tiling index matches (Polaris11, 4x Z24S8: depth macro mode
4, stencil macro mode 1), so sampled stencil reads back scrambled.

Set stencil_adjusted when the two macro tile modes differ. That clears
radeonsi's can_sample_s, so stencil sampling goes through the DB->CB copy;
TC-compatible HTILE and the surface layout are unchanged. Not specific to
big-endian hosts.

Against Debian mesa 25.0.7 with debian/patches/series applied.

--- a/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_surface.c
@@ -1633,6 +1633,20 @@
             if (AddrSurfInfoOut.tileMode >= ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1) {
                surf->u.legacy.stencil_tile_split = AddrSurfInfoOut.pTileInfo->tileSplitBytes;
             }
+
+            /* On GFX7-8 the DB applies the depth plane's macro tile mode
+             * (bank width, bank height, macro tile aspect) to both planes,
+             * while the texture unit derives the stencil plane's from the
+             * stencil tiling index. TC-compatible HTILE on MSAA gives depth
+             * a tile split that no stencil tiling index matches, so sampled
+             * stencil read back what the DB wrote with other bank parameters.
+             * When the two macro tile modes differ, sample stencil through
+             * the DB->CB copy instead.
+             */
+            if (info->gfx_level >= GFX7 && !only_stencil &&
+                AddrSurfInfoOut.tileMode >= ADDR_TM_2D_TILED_THIN1 &&
+                AddrSurfInfoOut.macroModeIndex != surf->u.legacy.macro_tile_index)
+               surf->u.legacy.stencil_adjusted = true;
          }
       }
    }
